Step 0 supports a Track B family, not Track A. The paper proves NP-completeness for the five-element Brandt semigroup \(B_2\) (Corollary 1.3 via Theorem 1.1), but the proposed planted XOR distribution has an efficient exact solver. The intended benchmark is therefore the no-tool gap between general GF(2) elimination and a short recurrence—not a distributional NP-hardness claim. I also found a canonical-diversity weakness in the draft: changing planted truth values only relabels generator choices, so I’m adding seed-dependent, certificate-preserving row identities whose structure survives canonicalization.
