The audited generator now has honest structural diversity: each seed includes a random necklace of redundant binary parity identities, obtained by XOR-composing adjacent cycle equations. They preserve the planted witness exactly, but unlike the planted right-hand side they are not erased by Boolean-value relabelling. Local gates G1–G8 pass, including 100 relabelling/complementation checks and 20/20 distinct canonical keys. The measured reference solve is 25,431 bit-XORs per shipping instance versus 299 for the recognized recurrence.
